# bundle_ambiguous.voc
#
# WHAT: edible greens/herbs that, after «molho de …», are AMBIGUOUS between a bunch
#       (bundle, open ɔ «mólho») and a sauce (closed o «môlho»): «colhi um molho de
#       salsa» (a bunch) vs «o bife tinha molho de salsa» (parsley sauce).
# WHERE USED: bifonia/scoring.py → score_verb(), pattern «molho de <thing>».
# EFFECT: a match here reads as BUNDLE only when a gathering/tying verb (see
#       bundle_verbs.voc) is in the left context; otherwise it defaults to the sauce
#       reading. Unambiguous bundles (chaves, lenha, …) live in bundle_things.voc and
#       fire unconditionally.
# HOW TO EXTEND: add greens that are sold/picked in bunches yet also occur as sauces.
#       One term per line, lowercase.
salsa
coentros
hortelã
hortelãs
manjericão
cebolinho
agrião
agriões
espinafres
couves
grelos
nabiças
brócolos
espargos
aipo
acelgas
rúcula
alfaces
cenouras
rabanetes
nabos
ervas
